<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Intrust ups capital ahead of Saflife offer.</title>
<headline>Intrust ups capital ahead of Saflife offer.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investec Investment Trust Ltd said on Friday it planned to to double its authorised share capital to 220,000 rand to enable it to hold a rights offer so it can follow its rights in Saflife Holdings Ltd's rights offer.</p>
<p>It said the Saflife offer would be held for the purpose of financial all or some of its purchase of a 34.9 percent stake in mining house JCI Ltd.</p>
<p>In a separate announcement on Friday, Saflife said it would be increasing its share capital by 100 million rand to facilitate the JCI purchase.</p>
<p>Saflife is the holding company of Capital Alliance Holdings Ltd, the leading member in a black consortium which last month clinched a deal to buy Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd's stake in JCI for 2.88 billion rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
